Meta's Reality Labs segment revenue decreased from 2022 to 2023.

According to the 2023 MD&A (Passage [11] and [13]), Reality Labs revenue in 2023 was $1,896 million, which was a decrease of $263 million, or 12%, compared to 2022 (when revenue was $2,159 million). The filing states that this decrease was "mostly driven by a net decrease in the volume of Meta Quest sales."
